# Us design system — token-only enforcement

This project uses the **Us Design System 3.0**. Treat it as the only source of
visual styling.

## Default profile: Web (digital)

**Unless the user explicitly asks for a presentation, deck, or `.pptx`:**

- Use the **Web profile**: Owners, IvyPresto Display, Public Sans
- Load Adobe Fonts kits `dbo7deg` and `rgx8kmt` + `us-tokens.css`
- Do **not** set `data-us-fonts="presentation"`
- Do **not** load Archivo / presentation Google Fonts stacks
- Do **not** apply presentation-only rules from `us-design-system.md` §9

Presentation profile applies **only when the user clearly specifies** that
deliverable type.

## Source files (required)

- **Values:** `us-tokens.css` (or `design-system/us-tokens.css`) — CSS custom properties from Figma
- **Rules:** `us-design-system.md` — typography, layout, components, non-negotiables
- **Figma:** [Us - Design System](https://www.figma.com/design/ObyTQ40kofwt9Ve44lzAQv) — if repo and Figma disagree, Figma wins

If these files are not present in the project, **stop** and ask the user to add
them from https://github.com/Us-develop/us-design-system before writing UI code.

## Hard rules

1. **Tokens only.** Every colour, spacing, radius, shadow, font size, line height,
   and font family must come from `us-tokens.css`. Use semantic 02 tokens for UI
   (`--content-body`, `--button-default-state-*`), not primitive palette entries.

2. **Web fonts by default.** Owners + IvyPresto Display + Public Sans (+ Material
   Symbols Outlined for UI icons, Font Awesome 6 Brands for social marks only).
   Never substitute Inter, Roboto, Arial, or other faces as a design choice.

3. **No invented styling.** No raw hex/px, no ad-hoc Tailwind colours, no custom
   shadows or gradients unless they exist as tokens. No letter-spacing.

4. **One profile per deliverable.** Web for digital products. Presentation (Archivo)
   only when explicitly requested — never mixed in the same deliverable.

5. **UI icons:** Material Symbols Outlined at weight 300 only. Use the documented
   icon tokens and sizes. No emoji for status or actions. Font Awesome Brands for
   social marks only.

6. **Feedback:** Success, error, warning, and info UI must use `--color-system-*`
   tokens and documented feedback patterns. Do not invent alert colours or emoji
   status indicators.

## When something is not defined — STOP

If you need a value, component pattern, or style that is **not** in the tokens or
rules:

- **Do not guess** or pick a “close” token
- **Do not continue** building that UI until resolved
- **Ask the user explicitly:** what is missing, why it blocks progress, and whether
  to update Figma/regenerate tokens, get designer input, or descope

Undefined = blocker. Improvisation is off-brand and not allowed.

## Before shipping UI

Verify: Web profile fonts loaded; no hard-coded colours/fonts/spacing outside
tokens; `data-us-mode` / `data-us-theme` used where needed; buttons are Shark not
purple; UI icons are Material Symbols (no emoji); feedback uses `--color-system-*`.
